course: dictionary
lesson: 16049
title: Strong, busy and full of energy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vigorous means strong, energetic and active. It describes doing something with lots of power and effort. Look at the clues around it: «After the vigorous game, Sam was puffed out and needed a drink of water.» A game that leaves you puffed out must be full of energy.
explain: The same word can describe a body, a plant or an argument. «Mia did vigorous exercise on the field, and her heart beat fast.» Then: «The young oak tree showed vigorous growth.» In both, vigorous means strong and full of life, but the thing that is strong is different each time.
explain: Test the meaning by swapping it in. Try «strong and energetic» in place of vigorous. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Vigorous means strong, energetic and active.
fact: «Vigorous exercise» means exercise, like running or swimming, that makes you breathe hard and your heart beat fast.
fact: Vigorous exercise helps to make the heart stronger.
fact: «Stir vigorously» means stir with strong, energetic movements, as in a science experiment.
fact: A «vigorous argument» is one where people argue with great energy and strength.
exercise: «After the vigorous game, the team was out of breath.» What does vigorous mean here? | Cold and wet | Lost and confused | Very quiet and calm | *Strong and energetic
exercise: The scientist said, «Stir the mixture vigorously.» How should you stir? | *With strong, energetic movements | With your eyes closed | Only once | Slowly and gently
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means strong and energetic: «The vigorous young plant grew tall in the sunshine.» | sunshine | *vigorous | young | plant
test: «Vigorous exercise makes your heart beat fast.» Which of these is an example of vigorous exercise? | Sleeping in bed | Reading a book quietly | *Running fast around the playground | Sitting still for a rest
test: «The vigorous growth of the bean plants surprised the class.» What does vigorous growth mean? | Not growing at all | Growing slowly and weakly | *Growing strongly and healthily | Growing only in the dark
exam: Mrs Patel said, «The debate was vigorous, with everyone speaking with energy.» What does vigorous suggest? | Broken and damaged | Quiet and shy | Bored and sleepy | *Strong, energetic and active
